agrams shows the vectors $3\\mathbf{a}$ and $-\\mathbf{a}$?"] [17592186097030 "Given that $4\\mathbf{a}-12\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\lambda (\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b})$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$."] [17592186097031 "Given that $\\lambda (-0.5\\mathbf{a}+6\\mathbf{b})$ and $\\mathbf{a}-12\\mathbf{b}$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$."] [17592186097032 "![](images/f5/f54e51921dfd2fb1b93bccec89553e174e2527866352626a5bf0846956b096bb.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the vector $\\mathbf{a}$. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}$?"] [17592186097247 "If a curve $\\mathcal{C}$ is given by $y = 2e^{x}(x + 1)$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x = 0$."] [17592186097260 "If a curve $\\mathcal{C}$ is given by $y = 8x^{3}\\sin x$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x = \\frac{π}{2}$."] [17592186106040 "The closed, positively oriented curve $C$ is defined as $\\mathbf{r}(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+4\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector on $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\frac{a(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+b(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}}{||{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $a(t).$"] [17592186106041 "The closed curve $C$ is defined as $\\mathbf{r}(t)=7\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+24\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector for $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\frac{a(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+b(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}}{||{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $b(t).$\n\n*Hint: Observe that $C$ is traversed clockwise.*"] [17592186106043 "The closed curve $C$ is defined as $\\mathbf{r}(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+8\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector for $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\frac{a(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+b(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}}{||{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $a(t).$\n\n*Hint: Observe that $C$ is traversed clockwise.*"] [17592186106060 "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=2xy,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$${∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186106063 "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=-3xz,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=\\sqrt{2}x+\\sqrt{2}y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$${∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186106094 "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=⟨k,1,1⟩$, $\\mathbf{b}=⟨5,0,4⟩$, and $\\mathbf{c}=⟨6,2,5⟩$ are coplanar."] [17592186106095 "Find $t$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{p}=⟨3,t,t⟩$, $\\mathbf{q}=⟨1,3,1⟩$, and $\\mathbf{r}=⟨1,1,3⟩$ are coplanar."] [17592186106309 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{x}=⟨3,5,0⟩$, $\\mathbf{y}=⟨3,2,0⟩$ and $\\mathbf{z}=⟨3,4,5⟩.$"] [17592186106310 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=⟨-3,0,-2⟩$, $\\mathbf{b}=⟨1,5,-3⟩$, and $\\mathbf{c}=⟨2,-1,4⟩$."] [17592186114970 "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\left(\\frac{1}{t-2}\\right)\\hspac