\hspace{0.222em}6-t,\\hspace{0.222em}7t⟩ \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}1-{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186115776 "Find the value of $(3\\mathbf{h}(t)-2\\mathbf{g}(t))^{'}$ at $t = 2$, if\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{h}(t) & =⟨2{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}t-3,\\hspace{0.222em}8+{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & =⟨{t}^{2}+2t,\\hspace{0.222em}8,\\hspace{0.222em}2{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186120071 "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}u,\\hspace{0.222em}{v}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}4v\\operatorname{cos}u⟩.$"] [17592186120073 "$${∬}_{D}\\boxed{\\phantom{AAAAAAAA}}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le \\pi \\}$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨2u\\operatorname{sin}v,\\hspace{0.222em}3u\\operatorname{cos}v,\\hspace{0.222em}u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le \\pi .$ What is the missing expression?"] [17592186120079 "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨-u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}u-2v,\\hspace{0.222em}3v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 4.$"] [17592186120091 "$${∬}_{D}\\boxed{\\phantom{AAAAAAAA}}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2\\}$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}u-{v}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{v}^{2}⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$ What is the missing expression?"] [17592186124943 "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f=\\mathbf{F},$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=-y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(3-x)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.$"] [17592186124955 "If $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)={e}^{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+{e}^{-t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))].$"] [17592186124956 "Evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]$ at $t=1$ given that\n$$\n\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y)=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+3y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+3y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}\n$$\nand\n$\\mathbf{r}(t)=t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.$"] [17592186124959 "If $f(x,y,z)=xy+yz+xz$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)=t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+{e}^{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+e\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))].$"] [17592186124960 "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+3xyz$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $\\mathbf{r}(t)=⟨{t}^{2},t+1,-t⟩$ at the point $t=1.$"] [17592186124961 "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $\\mathbf{r}(t)=⟨2\\sqrt{t},4t⟩$ at the point $t=1.$"] [17592186124962 "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=2x+{y}^{2}$ at the point $(0,1)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}=5\\mathbf{i}+2\\mathbf{j}.$"] [17592186124964 "Consider the function $g(x, y) = \\frac{x^{2}}{y}$. What is the rate of change of $g(x, y)$ at the point $(2, 1)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}=⟨-1,3⟩$?"] [17592186125024 "Find $f(x, y, z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)$, where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=2xy\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+({x}^{2}+2z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+2y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}$."] [17592186125061 "Find $f(x, y)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y)$, where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}x\\text{ }\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{sin}y\\text{ }\\mathbf{j}$."] [17592186125229 "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=(\\operatorname{cos}z+y\\operatorname{cos}x)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{sin}x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}-x\\operatorname{sin}z\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.$"] [17592186125246 "Evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]$ at $t=\\fra